@@ PR3 | Agile
A product owner measures success by the number of features delivered each quarter. What should the project manager encourage instead?
A) Measuring outcomes, such as customer retention, linked to the product goal
B) Measuring the number of story points delivered per developer each sprint
C) Measuring the number of hours the team logs in the time-tracking system
D) Measuring the percentage of the budget spent at the end of each quarter
= A
? Value is shown by outcomes, not outputs. Outcome metrics tell the team whether features actually achieve the product goal.

@@ PR3 | Predictive
At a phase gate, the updated business case shows that the expected annual savings have fallen from $2 million to $400,000 because of a change in energy prices. What should the project manager do?
A) Present the updated business case and options to the steering committee
B) Continue to the next phase, since the gate was planned months in advance
C) Recalculate the business case using the old energy prices to keep it positive
D) Cut the remaining budget by 80% without consulting the sponsor
= A
? Focusing on value means giving decision-makers accurate information about continued viability. Manipulating figures is unethical, and unilateral cuts bypass governance.

@@ PR3 | Hybrid
A compliance-driven logging feature adds no visible value for customers, so the product owner keeps ranking it low. The regulation takes effect in four months. How should it be prioritised?
A) As a high priority, since meeting the mandatory deadline protects the product
B) As a low priority, since customers will not notice whether the logging feature exists
C) As an optional item, to be implemented only if the team has spare capacity this year
D) As a separate project, to be delivered by the compliance department after the deadline
= A
? Mandatory compliance work protects the product's ability to operate and avoids penalties, so it carries high value even without visible customer features.

@@ PR3 | Agile | multi
Which two practices best maximise the value delivered by an agile team? (Choose two.)
A) Releasing frequently to obtain feedback from real users
B) Ordering the backlog by value, risk and learning
C) Maximising each developer's utilisation at all times
D) Completing all features before any release
E) Measuring success by lines of code written
= A, B
? Frequent releases and value-based ordering maximise value and learning. Utilisation, big-bang releases and code volume do not.

@@ PR4 | Predictive
The resource calendar shows that the only certified welder will be on holiday for two weeks during a critical-path activity. What should the project manager do?
