@@ PR5 | Predictive | fill
A fixed price incentive fee contract has a target cost of $200,000, a target profit of $20,000, a buyer/seller share ratio of 70/30 and a ceiling price of $230,000. The actual cost is $180,000. What is the final price paid? (Answer in dollars.)
= $206,000
? Underrun = $20,000; seller's share = 30% × 20,000 = $6,000; profit = 20,000 + 6,000 = $26,000; price = 180,000 + 26,000 = $206,000, below the ceiling.

@@ PR6 | Predictive
A project reports EV = $300,000, PV = $250,000 and AC = $330,000. How is it performing?
A) Ahead of schedule and over budget
B) Behind schedule and over budget
C) Ahead of schedule and under budget
D) Behind schedule and under budget
= A
? SV = 300,000 − 250,000 = +50,000 (ahead); CV = 300,000 − 330,000 = −30,000 (over budget).

@@ PR6 | Predictive
BAC = $600,000, EV = $240,000, AC = $300,000, CPI = 0.80 and SPI = 0.75. If both cost and schedule performance are expected to influence the remaining work, what is the EAC?
A) $900,000
B) $750,000
C) $660,000
D) $800,000
= A
? EAC = AC + (BAC − EV) / (CPI × SPI) = 300,000 + 360,000 / 0.60 = 300,000 + 600,000 = $900,000.

@@ PR6 | Agile
