@@ PR6 | Predictive
Two machines meet the requirements. Machine 1 costs $100,000 and $10,000 per year to operate. Machine 2 costs $80,000 and $16,000 per year. Both will be used for five years. Based on life-cycle cost, which should be chosen?
A) Machine 1, with a five-year cost of $150,000 versus $160,000
B) Machine 2, because its purchase price is $20,000 lower
C) Machine 2, with a five-year cost of $150,000 versus $160,000
D) Machine 1, because its purchase price is higher and quality is better
= A
