@@ PR6 | Predictive
Project A has an NPV of $120,000 and an IRR of 15%. Project B has an NPV of $150,000 and an IRR of 12%. Both exceed the 10% cost of capital, and only one can be funded. Which should be selected if the goal is to maximise value?
A) Project B, because it has the higher NPV
B) Project A, because it has the higher IRR
C) Neither, because their IRRs are too low
D) Both, by splitting the available funds
