An approved scope change adds three weeks of work to the critical path. What should the project manager do with the schedule baseline?
A) Update the baseline to reflect the approved change and communicate it
B) Keep the original baseline and report the change as a negative variance
C) Ask the team to absorb the three weeks without changing the baseline
D) Create a second, informal schedule that includes the extra work only
= A
? Approved changes are incorporated into the baselines so performance is measured against the current approved plan.

@@ PR9 | Predictive
The CPI has fallen from 0.98 to 0.94 to 0.90 over the last three months. What does trend analysis suggest?
A) Cost performance is deteriorating and the causes should be investigated now
B) Cost performance is improving, since the index is close to 1.0
C) No action is needed yet, since the CPI is still above the 0.85 threshold in the plan
D) The schedule is slipping, since CPI measures time performance
= A
? A consistent downward trend signals a worsening problem even before a threshold is breached; early investigation allows corrective action.

@@ PR9 | Agile
A team's velocity has varied between 15 and 40 points over the last six sprints. Stakeholders want a reliable forecast. What should the project manager do?
A) Investigate the causes of the variation with the team and forecast using a range
B) Use the highest velocity to give stakeholders the most optimistic forecast possible
C) Ask the team to deliver exactly 30 points every sprint from now on
D) Stop forecasting until velocity becomes stable without any intervention
= A
? Understanding the causes of instability helps the team stabilise, and forecasting with a range communicates uncertainty honestly.

@@ PR9 | Hybrid
The steering committee wants a small set of indicators to monitor a hybrid project. Which combination is most appropriate?
A) Milestone status, release burnup, budget versus actuals, and top risks
B) Each developer's daily logged hours and the number of emails sent per week
C) Only the Gantt chart for the predictive part of the project
D) The full list of backlog items and their story points
= A
? A concise mix of predictive and adaptive indicators gives the committee an integrated view without unnecessary detail.

@@ PR9 | Predictive
What is the main purpose of a performance review meeting in a predictive project?
A) To compare actual performance with the baseline and decide corrective actions
B) To evaluate each team member's personal performance for their annual appraisal
C) To approve the project charter and assign the project manager to the project
D) To celebrate milestones that the project has achieved during the past month
= A
? Performance reviews measure and analyse actual performance against the baselines and lead to corrective or preventive actions.

@@ PR9 | Agile
Which metric best indicates whether the quality of an agile team's releases is improving?
A) Escaped defects per release
B) Story points per sprint
C) Hours worked per sprint
D) Number of meetings held
= A
? Escaped defects — those found after release — directly reflect the quality reaching customers.

@@ PR9 | Predictive | multi
Which two earned value results show that a project is behind schedule? (Choose two.)
A) A negative schedule variance
B) An SPI below 1.0
C) A CPI below 1.0
D) A negative variance at completion
E) A TCPI above 1.0
= A, B
? SV < 0 and SPI < 1 indicate less work completed than planned. CPI, VAC and TCPI relate to cost performance.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
The design phase of a three-phase project is complete. What should the project manager do to close the phase?
A) Confirm the deliverables are accepted, capture lessons and get approval to proceed
B) Release the design team immediately so that their costs stop accumulating on the project
C) Start the construction phase at once to avoid losing momentum on site
D) Archive the design documents and wait for the sponsor to contact the team about next steps
= A
? Phase closure confirms deliverables, records lessons and passes through the governance gate before the next phase begins.

@@ PR10 | Agile
Before the final release of an internal application is handed over, what should be in place for the operations team?
A) An agreed support model, such as service levels, runbooks and escalation contacts
B) A promise that the development team will fix any problem at any time in the future
C) Access to the source code repository without any further explanation or training
D) Nothing, since operations teams are expected to support new systems independently
= A
? A clear support model and documentation enable operations to sustain the product after the project ends.

@@ PR10 | Hybrid
The project is closing, but its business benefits will be realised over the next 18 months. What should the project manager ensure?
A) Benefit tracking is formally handed over to the business benefit owner
B) The project remains open until all benefits have been fully realised
C) Benefit tracking is dropped, since the deliverables have been accepted
D) The team members continue to measure benefits in their spare time
= A
? Benefit ownership transfers to the business at closure so that measurement continues after the project ends.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
The contract allows the buyer to withhold 5% of the payments until a punch list of minor defects is completed. The seller asks for full payment now. What should the project manager do?
A) Follow the contract and release the retained amount after the punch list
B) Release the full payment to maintain a good relationship with the seller
C) Withhold the full final payment until the seller completes the punch list
D) Ask the seller to complete the punch list without any further payment
= A
? Retainage protects the buyer and is released according to the contract once the conditions are met.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
The final deliverable has been accepted and the contracts are closed. What should happen before the project team is released?
A) Final lessons are captured and knowledge and documents handed over
B) The team starts work on the next project while the closure report is pending
C) The project manager writes performance appraisals without team involvement
D) The sponsor approves each team member's next assignment personally
= A
? Lessons learned, handover and documentation are completed while the team is still available; then resources are released.

@@ PR10 | Agile
The project has formally closed, but stakeholders keep sending enhancement requests to the former team. What should happen to these requests?
A) They go to the product backlog or a new initiative
B) The former project team implements them informally as small favours
C) They are rejected permanently, since the product is now complete
D) They are added to the closed project's scope by the former project manager
= A
? After closure, new requests are handled through the product's ongoing backlog or a new project, with its own funding and governance.
